  if (from || to) match.occurredAt = { ...(from ? { $gte: from } : {}), ...(to ? { $lte: to } : {}) };

The declared indexes (models/LedgerEntry.js:124-128, plus field-level index:true at :41 and :56) are:
  { brandId, account, occurredAt: -1 }, { transactionId }, { settlementId }, { entryType, occurredAt: -1 }, { voucherClaimId }, { entryType }, { account }, { brandId }
There is no { account: 1, occurredAt: -1 }. The compound { brandId, account, occurredAt } is unusable here because brandId is absent from the match — PLATFORM_* rows carry no brandId at all (recordLedgerEntry.js:102-107 requires it only on VENDOR_PAYABLE).

models/Transaction.js:463-464:

    // buildSettlements' eligibility scan.
    transactionSchema.index({ settlementId: 1 }, { sparse: true });

The field it indexes has no default — `settlementId: settlementField` (Transaction.js:110) resolves to refField("Settlement") in models/validObjectId.js:5-16, which declares only `type`, `ref` and `validate`. Mongoose therefore leaves the path absent on every new transaction, and a sparse index does not index documents missing the field. The query is an equality on null — settlementClaims.js:57, `settlementId: null`, which by design matches both null and missing — and the planner will not use a sparse index for it, because doing so would silently omit the missing-field documents.

claimJobs.js:53-59 is the only sweep in the runner with no bound at all:

    const stale = await VoucherClaim.find({
      status: VOUCHER_CLAIM_STATUS.PENDING,
      isDeleted: false,
      createdAt: { $lte: cutoff },
    })
      .select("_id transactionId customerId brandId claimCode holdsUsageSlot")
      .lean();

Every other sweep caps itself — .limit(200) at settlementJobs.js:79/161/307, .limit(500) at 220, .limit(50) at claimJobs.js:170/233. Inside the loop each row does a Transaction.findById (claimJobs.js:68) and a synchronous getPaymentDetails call to Razorpay (claimJobs.js:81-83), and a lookup failure `continue`s without changing the claim's status (claimJobs.js:88-95), so that row is retried in full on the next tick.

services/settlements/buildSettlements.js:91-104 - no try/catch anywhere inside the loop:
  for (const brandId of brandIds) {
    const result = await buildForBrand({ brandId, periodStart, periodEnd, fundsReceivedBefore, minPayout, settings });
